{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"42df628c67eea4ea9dc4b02a27989ffeb60ce30829b97015b4d17ef888dcfa69","digest":{"component_or_area":"enrich drain gate (overlap queue)","key_entities":[".rebar/enrich-gate.json","overlap.queue.pending_enrichment","maybe_drain","overlap_drain_gate_budget_ms","enrich_drain.py","enrich_drain._append","enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain"],"problem_keywords":["drain gate latency","enrich queue","O(n) scaling","budget breach","write path overhead","metadata syscalls"],"propositions":["The enrich drain gate check is O(ticket count) because pending_enrichment walks every ticket directory and calls reduce_ticket three times per ticket, issuing ~24,000 metadata syscalls per write.","The gate consistently exceeds its declared 20 ms budget by 25x (486-740 ms warm) on stores with >4700 tickets, making the budget-breach warning fire on 100% of writes and rendering it noise.","Write latency degradation scales with concurrent agents (K agents = K simultaneous 24,000-syscall walks), causing positive feedback where the gate itself lengthens the write window.","pending_enrichment must remain O(1) for quiet stores via a marker under .rebar that degrades to a full scan only when genuinely needed, never missing a pending entry."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787536500021241001,"uuid":"d11f0e57-aed2-4faf-8e1c-d5b3e899c9c3"}